config TLSR_USB_POLL_TIMER
	bool "The 1 ms USB poll from Timer1's interrupt"
	depends on SOC_TLSR8278 && USB_DC_TELINK_B87 && !CIDOO_LED_KEY_MATRIX
	select USB_DC_TELINK_B87_EXTERNAL_POLL
	help
	  src/usb_poll_timer.c: Timer1 interrupts every millisecond and polls
	  the USB controller (USB_DC_TELINK_B87_EXTERNAL_POLL), instead of the
	  USB driver's kernel timer, whose timeout processing in the system
	  timer interrupt costs about ten times the poll. It owns Timer1. With
	  TLSR_USB_WIRED_POSITION_ONLY it starts when USB is enabled,
	  otherwise at init.

