config TLSR_BLE
	bool "Own BLE stack (experimental)"
	depends on SOC_TLSR8278 && FLASH && GPIO && !BT
	depends on DT_HAS_TELINK_B87_RADIO_ENABLED
	select SOC_TLSR8278_RADIO
	select TC32_AES128
	select TC32_RNG
	select TC32_P256
	help
	  src/ble: an own BLE peripheral stack on the TLSR8278 radio
	  (zephyr-tc32's radio driver, SOC_TLSR8278_RADIO). In the
	  BT position of the mode switch ("cidoo,mode-switch"): advertising,
	  connections (channel selection #1, the LL control procedures a
	  peripheral must answer), LL encryption with AES-CCM on the AES
	  block, L2CAP, SMP LE Secure Connections pairing (Passkey Entry or
	  Just Works, TLSR_BLE_SC_PASSKEY) with bonding (bonds in the storage
	  partition), and HID over GATT for ZMK's keyboard and
	  consumer reports (ZMK's BLE endpoint). Profiles on the channel
	  keys, the battery level, deep sleep while no host connects. Every
	  flash write holds the radio off.

if TLSR_BLE

config TLSR_BLE_SC_PASSKEY
	bool "Pairing by Passkey Entry: the keyboard types the passkey the host shows"
	default y
	help
	  Secure Connections with Passkey Entry, which protects against a
	  man in the middle: the host shows a passkey of up to six digits
	  and it is typed on the keyboard (the number row or the keypad),
	  then Enter; Backspace takes a digit back, Escape gives the pairing
	  up. The HID service and the notifications answer only over a link
	  encrypted with a key from such a pairing. Off: Just Works, with
	  no protection against a man in the middle; any host that connects
	  can pair.

config TLSR_BLE_CONN_PARAM_DELAY_MS
	int "Milliseconds after a connection before the parameter request (-1: none)"
	default 1000
	help
	  An L2CAP Connection Parameter Update Request with the
	  TLSR_BLE_CONN_* values. It waits while the link's encryption is
	  being started. GAP's Peripheral Preferred Connection Parameters
	  characteristic gives the same values.

config TLSR_BLE_CONN_INTERVAL
