if TLSR_P24

config TLSR_P24_AUTO_RX
	bool "The 2.4G link's receive started by the radio itself after each packet"
	help
	  Each packet goes out with the radio's send-then-receive command
	  (0xf00 = 0x87, the window in 0xf0a with 0xf03 bit 2), so the receive
	  starts a fixed time after the packet's end. Without it the RF
	  interrupt starts the receive when it sees the packet sent, later by
	  however long the interrupt had to wait. With it, a frame whose interrupt
	  has not run by the exchange's end is still taken.

