config TLSR_BLE_RNG_COLLECT
	bool "Collect for tc32_rng before advertising"
	default y
	help
	  The thread calls tc32_rng_collect() before each advertising run: on
	  a boot without a seed record the generator collects there until it
	  is ready (about 40 ms from the 32 kHz jitter and the ADC's noise),
	  so that a pairing's keys and a reconnection's session values are
	  there when asked for. When the collection gives up (its time limit,
	  or a 32 kHz count that stands still while the ADC credits nothing)
	  the thread does not advertise and collects again every second, the
	  advertising time limits running on. Off (for tests of
	  the refusal): the thread advertises anyway, and a request while the
	  generator is not ready fails, and the pairing or encryption start
	  with it.

endif # TLSR_BLE

config TLSR_RNG_STORE
